 "brief": "Tensor Products of Principal Unitary Representations of Quantum Lorentz Group and Askey-Wilson Polynomials E. Buffenoir ∗ — We study the tensor product of principal unitary representa tions of the",
 "extended": "**Tensor Products of Principal Unitary Representations of Quantum Lorentz Group and Askey-Wilson Polynomials E. Buffenoir ∗**\n\n*Laboratoire de Physique Mathématique et Théorique†*\n\n34 pp, 71 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We study the tensor product of principal unitary representa tions of the quantum Lorentz Group, prove a decomposition theorem and compute the associ ated intertwiners. We show that these intertwiners can be expressed in terms of complex continuations of 6 j symbols of Uq(su(2)). These intertwiners are expressed in terms of q-Racah polyno mials and Askey- Wilson polynomials. The orthogonality of these intertwine rs imply some relation mixing these two families of polynomials. The simplest of these rel ations is the orthogonality of Askey-Wilson Polynomials. Work supported by CNRS. ∗ e-mail:buﬀenoi@lpm.univ-montp2.fr † Laboratoire du CNRS UMR 5825 ‡ e-mail:roche@math.mit.edu § Laboratoire Propre du CNRS UPR 14 1\n\n**Outline.** Abstract; 1 Introduction; 2 Z × R} the set of principal; 2 (m2 +ρ2)dρ where; 2 Z,m +m′ +m′′ ∈ Z}. The aim of the present ar; 2 Z×] − π; 2 Deﬁnition and properties of various continua; 2.1 Intertwiners and 6j(0) of Uq(su(2)); 2 Z+, ∀m ∈ 1; 2 Z we deﬁne; 2.2 Deﬁnitions and properties of continuation ; 2 Z+, and for a suﬃciently large half-integer ; 2 Z+,X 1,X 2,Y 1,Y 2,Z 1 ∈ C − 1; 2 Z+,X 1 −X2 ∈ 1; 2 Z,Y 1 −Y2 ∈ 1; 2 Z and deﬁned by; 2.3 Quantum Lorentz group, Principal Unitary R; 2 Z+ the elements",
